From 0974ae15f5c8e3f8d920984730a0c4afe2854057 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:05:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: map a 32-bit image below the WoW64 limit.

The main image is mapped before init_peb sets user_space_wow_limit, so
map_image_view tries no range below it and maps "any suitable address".
Upstream's free-area search starts low and finds one below 2 GiB; the
console's map_view prefers its reserved area above 4 GiB, and a 32-bit
program was mapped at 0x1000000000: its 32-bit PEB then said
ImageBaseAddress 0 (the low half), and 32-bit ntdll faulted in
set_wow64_environment, reading the image's NT header at address 4
(PS5_Proton m3-pe32-2026-10-07-06 and -08).

A 32-bit image is now held below the WoW64 limit, the image's own
large-address-aware flag deciding it before init_peb has.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 1b495ef..b768b45 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4029,6 +4029,17 @@ static NTSTATUS map_image_view( struct file_view **view_ret, struct pe_image_inf
 
     limit_low = max( limit_low, (ULONG_PTR)address_space_start );  /* make sure the DOS area remains free */
     if (!limit_high) limit_high = (ULONG_PTR)user_space_limit;
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__) && defined(_WIN64)
+    /* A 32-bit image runs as 32-bit code: it stays below the WoW64 limit, also
+     * for the main image, which is mapped before init_peb sets that limit from
+     * the image's own flag. Upstream finds a low address then because the
+     * search starts low; the console's map_view prefers its reserved area
+     * above 4 GiB, and the program was mapped at 0x1000000000, so the 32-bit
+     * PEB's ImageBaseAddress was 0 (docs/IA32_DESIGN.md, M3). */
+    if (!is_machine_64bit( image_info->machine ))
+        limit_high = min( limit_high, user_space_wow_limit ? user_space_wow_limit :
+                          ((image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE) ? limit_4g : limit_2g) - 1 );
+#endif
 
     /* first try the specified base */
 
